From e9b98100993007588f0af48a2c654af85b41f0bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Mar 2026 14:04:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/13] SettingsProvider: Fix NPE in SSAID migration on legacy
 vendor partitions

migrateAllLegacySettingsIfNeededLocked() creates system, secure, and
global settings states via migrateLegacySettingsForUserLocked(), but
does not create the SSAID settings state. When the subsequent upgrade
path reaches version 136->137, getSsaidSettingsLocked() returns null
and the code crashes with an NPE at getSettingLocked().

This affects GSI installations over old vendor partitions (e.g.
Android 11) where isDeviceUpgrading() returns true but no SSAID XML
file exists yet. The normal boot path (ensureSettingsForUserAndDeviceLocked)
correctly ensures SSAID state before upgrading, but the legacy
migration path was missing this step.

Fix by ensuring SSAID settings state in migrateAllLegacySettingsIfNeededLocked
before running the upgrade, matching the normal boot path. Also add a
defensive null check at the usage site as defense-in-depth.

This is an AOSP bug present in stock Android, not a GrapheneOS
regression.
